  "body": "## What changed\n\nIntroduce the native `my-claude-code` / `mcc-*` command family while keeping every\nlegacy `fcc-*` / `free-claude-code` command working as an alias for the same\nimplementation. This is the migration bridge: both command families are\ninterchangeable entry points into one shared codebase.\n\n- Register `mcc-server`, `my-claude-code`, `mcc-init`, `mcc-claude`,\n  `mcc-claude-old`, `mcc-codex`, `mcc-pi`, `mcc-chatgpt-oauth-login`, and\n  `mcc-compact-log` in `[project.scripts]`, each pointing at the existing\n  implementation.\n- Add `core/identity.py` with a neutral `ToolOwner` model (`LEGACY_OWNER` /\n  `NATIVE_OWNER`) that centralises the two command families, display names,\n  stable launchers, and receipt/extras mapping.\n- Make `core/version.py` owner-aware: `package_version()` and the new\n  `distribution_name()` try the native distribution first and fall back to the\n  legacy name.\n- Derive the `--version` label from `owner_for_invocation()`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Targeted suite: 15 passed (`tests/core/test_identity.py`), plus 87 in\n  `tests/cli/test_entrypoints.py` + `tests/core/test_version.py`.\n- `ruff format --check`, `ruff check`, `ty check` clean on changed files.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- The compatibility wheel, installer/uninstaller dual-identity handling, and\n  updater owner-awareness are planned for a follow-up release; this change\n  focuses on the command-family bridge and the neutral identity model.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
