     "date": "2026-08-11T12:24:21Z"
    },
    "message": "@\nfeat: add My Claude Code command family alongside legacy aliases (#81)\n\nIntroduce the native my-claude-code / mcc-* command family while keeping\nevery legacy fcc-* / free-claude-code command working as an alias for the\nsame implementation. This is the migration bridge: both command families\nare interchangeable entry points into one shared codebase.\n\n- Register mcc-server, my-claude-code, mcc-init, mcc-claude, mcc-claude-old,\n  mcc-codex, mcc-pi, mcc-chatgpt-oauth-login, and mcc-compact-log in\n  [project.scripts], each pointing at the existing implementation.\n- Add core/identity.py with a neutral ToolOwner model (LEGACY_OWNER /\n  NATIVE_OWNER) that centralises the two command families, display names,\n  stable launchers, and receipt/extras mapping so literals stop scattering\n  across the installer, self-updater, and launchers.\n- Make core/version.py owner-aware: package_version() and the new\n  distribution_name() try the native distribution first and fall back to the\n  legacy name, so either owner reports the correct installed metadata.\n- Derive the --version label from owner_for_invocation() so native\n  invocations report \"my-claude-code X.Y.Z\" and legacy invocations report\n  \"free-claude-code X.Y.Z\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n@",
